@* CreateGroup.razor — Salary-budget feature, Step 6

   Staff-facing customer-group creation page at route `/Admin/Groups/Create`.
   Reached from the "Create group" button on /Admin/Groups. Role-gated to
   Admin / Manager via [Authorize(Roles=...)] as defense-in-depth. The
   page-level gate is the first cut; the CreateCustomerGroupCommand
   handler enforces stricter rules server-side (Manager or Admin only).

   PURPOSE:
     Lets admins/managers create a new customer group so the salary-budget
     feature can be exercised end-to-end (a user must have a GroupId to
     be subject to budget + currency-matching checks). Creating a group
     also bulk-applies a default purchase-limit row of 1 to every existing
     product (Step 5 wiring), so customers in the new group immediately
     have a sensible per-product cap.

   FORM FIELDS:
     1. Name              (required, 1-100 chars; must be unique)
     2. Salary Amount     (required, >= 0)
     3. Salary Currency   (required, 3-letter ISO 4217 — dropdown with the
                           most common currencies; user can also type a
                           custom 3-letter code via AllowCustomValue)

   STYLE PARITY WITH CREATEUSER / CREATEPRODUCT:
     Mirrors CreateUser.razor's structure and styling:
       - Same .create-grid layout (2fr form + 1fr help panel, collapses on
         narrow screens).
       - Same .form-section vertical-stack of fields.
       - Same .form-actions row at the bottom (Cancel + Create).
       - Same .form-error banner for server-side errors.
       - Same .price-row pattern for amount + currency side-by-side.
       - Same currency dropdown as CreateProduct (so the admin sees the
         same currency list across both Create flows — consistency matters).

   BULK-DEFAULT WARNING:
     Creating a group bulk-applies a default purchase limit to every
     existing product. The help panel on the right explains this so the
     admin understands the impact before clicking Create. If the catalog
     is large (> 1000 products), creation will take a few seconds — the
     button shows a spinner during the round-trip.

   CURRENCY NOTE:
     The currency chosen here ALSO defines what currency of products the
     group's customers may buy. Currency match is enforced on EVERY cart
     mutation, in EVERY limit mode (including CountOnly), by
     IPurchaseLimitPolicy. The currency CANNOT be changed after creation
     (changing currency would invalidate already-purchased products
     priced in the old currency) — to "change currency", deactivate this
     group and create a new one. The help panel calls this out.

   LOCALIZATION:
     All user-visible strings via IStringLocalizer<CreateGroup> (Loc).
     Keys defined in CreateGroup.en-US.resx + CreateGroup.fa-IR.resx.

   ANTIFORGERY:
     Required — EditForm with OnValidSubmit. Blazor Server circuits
     already have an anti-forgery token established at circuit-start;
     EditForm validates it automatically. *@

@page "/Admin/Groups/Create"
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager")]
@using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations
@using System.Globalization
@using System.Text
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Forms
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Customers.Commands.CreateCustomerGroup
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<CreateGroup> Loc
@inject ToastService Toast

<PageTitle>@Loc["PageTitle"]</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            .create-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
                gap: 2rem;
                align-items: start;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 992px) {
                .create-grid {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                    gap: 1.25rem;
                }
            }

            .form-section {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 1.25rem;
            }

            .salary-row {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                align-items: flex-end;
            }

                .salary-row .salary-amount {
                    flex: 1 1 auto;
                }

                .salary-row .salary-currency {
                    flex: 0 0 220px;
                }

            .form-actions {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                justify-content: flex-end;
                margin-top: 1rem;
            }

            .form-error {
                margin-bottom: 1rem;
            }

            /* Help panel on the right — same pattern as CreateUser.razor.
                                       Sticky on desktop so it stays visible while the user scrolls
                                       the form on small screens. */
            .help-panel {
                position: sticky;
                top: 1rem;
            }

                /* Section title — small heading inside the help card with
                                           a leading icon. Mirrors the .section-title pattern used
                                           on the Settings page's cards. */
                .help-panel .section-title {
                    display: flex;
                    align-items: center;
                    gap: 0.5rem;
                    font-weight: 600;
                    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
                }

                .help-panel ul {
                    margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0;
                    padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    line-height: 1.7;
                }

                .help-panel li {
                    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
                }

            @@media (max-width: 992px) {
                .help-panel {
                    position: static;
                }
            }

            /* RTL fallback for RadzenNumeric — the inner input is forced
                                       LTR so the caret + digit grouping reads correctly in both
                                       LTR and RTL layouts. Same pattern as CreateProduct.razor. */
            .salary-row .rz-numeric .rz-textbox {
                direction: ltr;
                text-align: left;
            }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Breadcrumb + back button ──
       ButtonStyle.Secondary + Variant.Outlined (NOT ButtonStyle.Light) —
       the Light variant renders as flat gray text on light themes,
       which is invisible. Secondary gives a visible outlined button
       that works on both light and dark themes. Same pattern as
       CreateUser.razor's back button. *@
    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem">
        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["BackToManageGroups"]"
                      Icon="arrow_back"
                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                      Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                      Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Groups", forceLoad: false))" />
    </RadzenStack>

    @* ── Page header ── *@
    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
        <RadzenIcon Icon="group_add" Style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--rz-primary);" />
        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["PageHeading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
    </RadzenStack>

    @* ── Main form ── *@
    <div class="create-grid">
        @* LEFT — form fields *@
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.5rem;">
            <EditForm Model="@_model"
                      OnValidSubmit="@HandleSubmitAsync"
                      OnInvalidSubmit="@HandleInvalidSubmit"
                      FormName="createGroup">
                <DataAnnotationsValidator />

                @* Server-side error banner (e.g. "A group with name 'X' already exists.") *@
                @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_submitError))
                {
                    <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                                 Text="@_submitError"
                                 AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                                 Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                 ShowIcon="true"
                                 Class="form-error" />
                }

                <div class="form-section">
                    @* ── Name ── *@
                    <div>
                        <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldName"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                            <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_model.Name"
                                           Placeholder="@Loc["FieldNamePlaceholder"]"
                                           TValue="string"
                                           Style="width: 100%;" />
                        </RadzenFormField>
                        <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-top: 0.25rem;">
                            @Loc["NameHint"]
                        </RadzenText>
                    </div>

                    @* ── Salary Amount + Currency ──
                       Side-by-side row: amount takes the remaining space,
                       currency is fixed 220px. Same .salary-row pattern as
                       CreateProduct.razor's .price-row.

                       AMOUNT TEXTBOX:
                         We use a RadzenTextBox bound to a STRING field
                         (_salaryAmountText), NOT a RadzenNumeric bound
                         to a decimal. Three reasons:
                           1. IRR amounts are whole Rial — we never want
                              to show 2 decimal digits. RadzenNumeric
                              with TValue=decimal defaults to 2 decimals
                              and there's no clean way to make Decimals
                              conditional on the currency at runtime.
                           2. We need thousands separators (N0 format).
                              RadzenNumeric.Format="N0" DOES add them,
                              BUT only when the input is NOT focused —
                              and even then .NET's NativeDigits is
                              informational-only (see CultureFormat.cs
                              header comment), so the digits come out
                              ASCII in fa-IR mode.
                           3. We need Persian digits (۰-۹) when the UI
                              culture is fa-IR. The only reliable way
                              to get Persian digits out of .NET is the
                              manual swap in CultureFormat.ToCultureDigits.
                              That swap has to happen on a STRING we
                              control — not inside RadzenNumeric.
                         So: bind a string, format on blur, parse on
                         focus. The user edits the raw invariant number
                         while the input is focused (easy typing, no
                         separators to fight with), and sees the
                         formatted (thousand-separated, Persian-digit)
                         form when not editing. NOTE: the format is
                         re-evaluated whenever the currency dropdown
                         changes (OnSalaryCurrencyChanged) so switching
                         between IRR (N0) and USD (N2) re-formats the
                         displayed amount appropriately. *@
                    <div>
                        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["FieldSalary"]"
                                    TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;" />

                        <div class="salary-row">
                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldAmount"]" Class="salary-amount" Style="width: 100%;">
                                <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_salaryAmountText"
                                               TValue="string"
                                               Style="width: 100%; direction: ltr; text-align: left;"
                                               Placeholder="@Loc["FieldAmountPlaceholder"]"
                                               @onfocus="OnSalaryAmountFocus"
                                               @onblur="OnSalaryAmountBlur" />
                            </RadzenFormField>

                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldCurrency"]" Class="salary-currency" Style="width: 100%;">
                                <RadzenDropDown @bind-Value="_model.SalaryCurrency"
                                                Data="@_currencyOptions"
                                                TValue="string"
                                                TextProperty="DisplayName"
                                                ValueProperty="Code"
                                                AllowCustomValue="true"
                                                AllowFiltering="true"
                                                Placeholder="@Loc["CurrencyPlaceholder"]"
                                                Change="@(args => OnSalaryCurrencyChanged(args?.ToString()))"
                                                Style="width: 100%;" />
                            </RadzenFormField>
                        </div>

                        <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-top: 0.25rem;">
                            @Loc["SalaryHint"]
                        </RadzenText>
                    </div>

                    @* ── Form actions ── *@
                    <div class="form-actions">
                        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["CancelButton"]"
                                      Icon="close"
                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                                      Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                      Disabled="@_isSubmitting"
                                      Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Groups", forceLoad: false))" />

                        <RadzenButton ButtonType="ButtonType.Submit"
                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                      Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                      Disabled="@_isSubmitting">
                            @* ChildContent (this @if block) takes precedence over
                               the Text= and Icon= parameters on RadzenButton —
                               once any child content exists, Radzen stops rendering
                               Text/Icon. So we render the icon + text EXPLICITLY
                               here, swapping to a spinner while submitting. This
                               is the only way to keep the button text visible
                               AND show an inline spinner during submit. *@
                            @if (_isSubmitting)
                            {
                                <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false"
                                                           Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate"
                                                           Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Small"
                                                           Style="margin-inline-end: 0.5rem;" />
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="check" Style="margin-inline-end: 0.5rem;" />
                            }
                            <span>@Loc["CreateButton"]</span>
                        </RadzenButton>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </EditForm>
        </RadzenCard>

        @* RIGHT — help panel. Explains:
             - What "monthly budget" means (spending ceiling per user per month).
             - What "currency" means (also defines what currency of products
               the group's customers may buy — enforced on every cart mutation).
             - Bulk-default behavior (creating a group bulk-applies a default
               purchase-limit of 1 to every existing product).
             - Currency is permanent (cannot be changed after creation —
               to "change currency", deactivate this group and create a new one). *@
        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
            <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Outlined" Class="help-panel" Style="padding: 1.25rem;">
                <div class="section-title">
                    <RadzenIcon Icon="help_outline" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                    <span>@Loc["HelpCardTitle"]</span>
                </div>
                <ul>
                    <li>@Loc["HelpLine_Budget"]</li>
                    <li>@Loc["HelpLine_Currency"]</li>
                    <li>@Loc["HelpLine_BulkDefault"]</li>
                    <li>@Loc["HelpLine_Permanent"]</li>
                </ul>
            </RadzenCard>
        </RadzenStack>
    </div>
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── State ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// The form model. Bound via EditForm + DataAnnotationsValidator —
    /// the [Required] + [Range] attributes below provide the FIRST wave
    /// of validation (fires in OnValidSubmit / OnInvalidSubmit). The
    /// CreateCustomerGroupCommandValidator provides the SECOND wave
    /// server-side via Wolverine's pipeline (more business-rule checks:
    /// exact length bounds, currency 3-letter format). The handler
    /// itself provides the THIRD wave (name uniqueness in the DB).
    /// </summary>
    private sealed class CreateGroupForm
    {
        [Required(ErrorMessage = "ValidationError_NameRequired")]
        [StringLength(100, ErrorMessage = "ValidationError_NameLength")]
        public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;

        [Required(ErrorMessage = "ValidationError_AmountRequired")]
        [Range(0, double.MaxValue, ErrorMessage = "ValidationError_AmountRange")]
        public decimal SalaryAmount { get; set; } = 0;

        [Required(ErrorMessage = "ValidationError_CurrencyRequired")]
        [StringLength(3, MinimumLength = 3, ErrorMessage = "ValidationError_CurrencyLength")]
        public string SalaryCurrency { get; set; } = "IRR";
    }

    private readonly CreateGroupForm _model = new();

    private bool _isSubmitting;
    private string? _submitError;

    /// <summary>
    /// The text shown in the Salary Amount textbox. Bound to a STRING (not a
    /// decimal) so we can format it ourselves: thousands separators + Persian
    /// digits (in fa-IR mode) + 0 decimal places when the currency is IRR.
    /// See the comment block above the textbox in the markup for the full
    /// rationale of why RadzenNumeric + decimal wasn't suitable.
    ///
    /// SYNC CONTRACT:
    ///   - On focus: parsed to a decimal, then re-stored as the raw invariant
    ///     string (e.g. "1234567") so the user can edit easily without
    ///     fighting separators.
    ///   - On blur: parsed to a decimal, then re-stored as the formatted
    ///     display value (e.g. "1,234,567" in en-US, "۱٬۲۳۴٬۵۶۷" in fa-IR),
    ///     AND propagated to _model.SalaryAmount for form submission.
    ///   - On currency change: re-formatted (because IRR uses N0, others N2).
    ///   - On submit (HandleSubmitAsync): re-parsed from text to decimal
    ///     defensively, in case the user clicked Save while the textbox was
    ///     still focused (so onblur hadn't fired yet).
    /// </summary>
    private string _salaryAmountText = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// The most common ISO 4217 currency codes — identical to
    /// CreateProduct.razor's _currencyOptions so the admin sees the
    /// same currency list across both Create flows. The user can also
    /// type a custom 3-letter code via the dropdown's AllowCustomValue.
    ///
    /// DISPLAY FORMAT (per the user's spec):
    ///   - In fa-IR (Persian) UI:  "IRR (ریال)"
    ///   - In en-US (English) UI:  "IRR (Rial)"
    /// Only the matching language's name is shown — the code is always
    /// Latin (ISO 4217) so it's recognizable in both UIs.
    /// </summary>
    private readonly List<CurrencyOption> _currencyOptions = new()
    {
        new() { Code = "IRR", EnglishName = "Rial",           PersianName = "ریال" },
        new() { Code = "USD", EnglishName = "US dollar",      PersianName = "دلار" },
        new() { Code = "EUR", EnglishName = "Euro",           PersianName = "یورو" },
        new() { Code = "GBP", EnglishName = "Pound sterling", PersianName = "پوند" },
        new() { Code = "JPY", EnglishName = "Japanese yen",   PersianName = "ین ژاپن" },
        new() { Code = "CNY", EnglishName = "Chinese yuan",   PersianName = "یوآن چین" },
        new() { Code = "AED", EnglishName = "UAE dirham",     PersianName = "درهم امارات" },
        new() { Code = "TRY", EnglishName = "Turkish lira",   PersianName = "لیر ترکیه" },
        new() { Code = "CAD", EnglishName = "Canadian dollar", PersianName = "دلار کانادا" },
        new() { Code = "AUD", EnglishName = "Australian dollar", PersianName = "دلار استرالیا" }
    };

    private sealed class CurrencyOption
    {
        public string Code { get; init; } = string.Empty;
        public string EnglishName { get; init; } = string.Empty;
        public string PersianName { get; init; } = string.Empty;

        /// <summary>
        /// Culture-aware display string — same logic as CreateProduct's
        /// CurrencyOption.DisplayName. Re-evaluated on every render so
        /// language switches pick up without rebuilding the list.
        /// </summary>
        public string DisplayName =>
            CultureInfo.CurrentUICulture.Name
                .StartsWith("fa", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                ? $"{Code} ({PersianName})"
                : $"{Code} ({EnglishName})";
    }

    // ── Submit handlers ───────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Called when EditForm validation passes. Dispatches the
    /// CreateCustomerGroupCommand via Wolverine. On success, navigates
    /// back to /Admin/Groups with a success toast. On failure, surfaces
    /// the server error in the form-error banner.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleSubmitAsync()
    {
        _submitError = null;
        _isSubmitting = true;

        try
        {
            // Trim whitespace from name + currency before submission —
            // prevents " ABC " from being treated as different from "ABC".
            _model.Name = _model.Name.Trim();
            _model.SalaryCurrency = _model.SalaryCurrency.Trim().ToUpperInvariant();

            // Defensive re-parse of the salary textbox. Normally OnBlur
            // fires before the submit button's click handler does, but a
            // JS-initiated submit or Enter-key submit could race. Parsing
            // here too guarantees _model.SalaryAmount reflects whatever
            // the user typed, even if OnBlur hasn't run yet.
            //
            // If parsing fails (user typed garbage), we leave _model.SalaryAmount
            // alone — DataAnnotationsValidator's [Range] attribute will catch
            // an out-of-range value, and the OnInvalidSubmit handler will
            // surface the validation error. We DON'T set SalaryAmount to 0
            // because that would mask the real "invalid input" issue with
            // a misleading "amount 0" success.
            if (TryParseAmount(_salaryAmountText, out var parsedAmount))
            {
                _model.SalaryAmount = parsedAmount;
            }

            var command = new CreateCustomerGroupCommand(
                _model.Name,
                _model.SalaryAmount,
                _model.SalaryCurrency);

            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<Guid>>(command);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(Loc["SuccessTitle"], summary: Loc["SuccessSummary"]);
                Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Groups", forceLoad: false);
            }
            else
            {
                // The handler returns friendly, user-actionable messages
                // (e.g. "A customer group with the name 'X' already exists.
                // Choose a different name.") — surface verbatim.
                _submitError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_Generic"];
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            _submitError = Loc["Error_Generic"];
        }
        finally
        {
            _isSubmitting = false;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Called when EditForm validation FAILS (e.g. user submitted with an
    /// empty Name). We just clear the previous server-side error banner
    /// so the user sees the field-level errors only (no stale banner).
    /// The DataAnnotationsValidator already renders field-level errors
    /// next to each RadzenFormField.
    /// </summary>
    private Task HandleInvalidSubmit()
    {
        _submitError = null;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    // ── Salary amount textbox helpers ────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Formats a decimal salary amount for DISPLAY in the textbox (i.e.
    /// when the input is NOT focused). Returns a string with:
    ///   - Persian digits (۰-۹) when the UI culture is fa-IR, ASCII (0-9)
    ///     otherwise — via <see cref="CultureFormat.ToCultureDigits"/>.
    ///   - Thousands separators ("," in en-US, "٬" in fa-IR — also handled
    ///     by ToCultureDigits since the .NET N0 format produces commas
    ///     and ToCultureDigits swaps them).
    ///   - 0 decimal places when the currency is IRR (whole-Rial — Iran's
    ///     currency has no fractional unit in practice for salary values).
    ///     2 decimal places for other currencies (USD, EUR, etc.).
    /// </summary>
    private string FormatSalaryForDisplay(decimal amount)
    {
        var isIrr = string.Equals(_model.SalaryCurrency, "IRR",
            StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
        // N0 = no decimals, with thousands separators.
        // N2 = 2 decimal places, with thousands separators.
        // InvariantCulture produces ASCII digits + comma separators; we then
        // run ToCultureDigits to swap them for Persian digits + ٬ separator
        // when the UI culture is fa-IR.
        var fmt = isIrr ? "N0" : "N2";
        return CultureFormat.ToCultureDigits(
            amount.ToString(fmt, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Parses a string the user typed into the salary amount textbox into
    /// a decimal. Accepts:
    ///   - ASCII digits "0"-"9"
    ///   - Persian digits "۰"-"۹" (converted to ASCII before parsing)
    ///   - Thousands separators "," and "٬" (ignored)
    ///   - Decimal separator "." (ASCII) or "٫" (Persian) — both converted
    ///     to "." for the InvariantCulture parser
    ///   - Leading/trailing whitespace (trimmed)
    /// Returns false on any parse failure (caller decides what to do —
    /// usually leaves _model.SalaryAmount alone and lets validation catch
    /// the bad input).
    /// </summary>
    private static bool TryParseAmount(string? input, out decimal amount)
    {
        amount = 0m;
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(input)) return false;

        // Normalize: strip separators, convert Persian digits/decimal-point
        // to ASCII equivalents, then parse with InvariantCulture.
        var sb = new StringBuilder(input.Length);
        foreach (var c in input.Trim())
        {
            if (c == ',' || c == '٬') continue;       // thousands separator
            if (c == '٫') sb.Append('.');              // Persian decimal point
            else if (c >= '۰' && c <= '۹')
                sb.Append((char)('0' + (c - '۰')));    // Persian digit → ASCII
            else sb.Append(c);
        }

        return decimal.TryParse(sb.ToString(),
            NumberStyles.Number, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, out amount);
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Fired when the salary amount textbox gains focus. Switches the
    /// displayed text from the formatted (thousand-separated, Persian-digit)
    /// form to the raw invariant number so the user can edit easily
    /// without fighting separators. If the current text doesn't parse
    /// (e.g. user typed garbage that we couldn't format on a previous
    /// blur), we leave the text alone so the user can see what they typed.
    /// </summary>
    private void OnSalaryAmountFocus()
    {
        if (TryParseAmount(_salaryAmountText, out var amount))
        {
            // InvariantCulture produces ASCII digits + "." decimal separator
            // — the safest form for free-text editing. No thousands separators
            // (they'd just get in the way while typing).
            _salaryAmountText = amount.ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
        }
        // else: leave the text alone so the user can fix whatever they typed.
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Fired when the salary amount textbox loses focus. Parses the current
    /// text to a decimal, propagates it to <see cref="CreateGroupForm.SalaryAmount"/>
    /// (so the form's [Range] validation can fire on the real value), and
    /// re-formats the displayed text with thousand separators + Persian
    /// digits (in fa-IR) + 0 decimals (in IRR). If parsing fails, we leave
    /// both the text and _model.SalaryAmount alone — DataAnnotationsValidator
    /// will surface a validation error via the [Required] + [Range] attrs.
    /// </summary>
    private void OnSalaryAmountBlur()
    {
        if (TryParseAmount(_salaryAmountText, out var amount))
        {
            _model.SalaryAmount = amount;
            _salaryAmountText = FormatSalaryForDisplay(amount);
        }
        // else: leave text + SalaryAmount alone — validation will fire on submit.
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Fired when the salary currency dropdown changes. The new currency
    /// code is propagated to <see cref="CreateGroupForm.SalaryCurrency"/>
    /// (redundant with @bind-Value, but eliminates any timing ambiguity
    /// with binding propagation — same pattern as EditGroup's status filter).
    /// Then the displayed amount is re-formatted, because IRR uses N0 (no
    /// decimals) and other currencies use N2 (2 decimals) — switching
    /// currency while the textbox shows a formatted value would otherwise
    /// leave stale precision.
    /// </summary>
    private void OnSalaryCurrencyChanged(string? value)
    {
        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(value))
        {
            _model.SalaryCurrency = value.Trim().ToUpperInvariant();
        }

        // Re-format the displayed amount under the new currency.
        if (TryParseAmount(_salaryAmountText, out var amount))
        {
            _salaryAmountText = FormatSalaryForDisplay(amount);
        }
    }
}